{{Quote|We have three ''Sheathipede''-class shuttles, but they have no weapons.|General Kalani|<ref name="The Last Battle" />}}
The '''''Sheathipede''-class transport shuttle''',<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> also known as the '''''Sheathipede''-class shuttle'''<ref name="The Last Battle" /> and as the '''Neimoidian escort shuttle''',<ref name="Databank" /> was a short-range [[transport]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> used by the [[Trade Federation]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="Databank" /> Multiple versions of the shuttle existed including a [[Sheathipede-class Type B shuttle|a larger version]] with an extended midsection, weaponized and weaponless variants, and a droid-pilot variant.<ref name="Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles]]''</ref> The Sheathipede shuttle also shared many of its characteristics with the much larger [[Maxillipede shuttle]].

==Characteristics==
A product of [[Haor Chall Engineering Corporation]], the ''Sheathipede''-class was a [[transport]] [[shuttle]] with a curved hull and pincer-like landing gears, which lowered from the ship's rounded belly,<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> and the shuttle's shape roughly resembled the [[Neimoidian soldier beetle]].<ref name="Rise">''[[Rise of the Separatists]]''</ref> At a length of 14.4 [[meter]]s,<ref name="Databank" /> the shuttle was powered by two engines and featured an egress hatchway at the rear.<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> Some models replaced the [[cockpit]] with an expanded passenger cabin, and were flown by automatic [[pilot]]s.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" />

[[File:Armed_Sheathipede_variant.png|thumb|left|200px|A Sheathipede model armed with laser weaponry.]]
Stock ''Sheathipede'' shuttles were unarmed and only possessed a basic [[Deflector shield generator|shield generator]], meaning that, rather than relying on strength, the ships relied on speed and a small [[sensor]] cross-section to get to a destination. Many of the shuttles used by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] were upgraded with improved shielding, better armor, and larger engines.<ref name="Rise" /> While uncommon, a decent number had light weapons added, typically in the form a trio of [[laser cannon]]s.<ref name="SWE">{{SWE|technology|neimoidianshuttle|Neimoidian escort shuttle}}</ref> These armed ''Sheathipedes'' were used to move very valuable materiel through hostile locations and transport high-[[Military rank|ranking]] [[officer]]s and officials.<ref name="Rise" />

==History==
===Early history===
The ''Sheathipede''-class shuttle was a short-range transport<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> and escort shuttle<ref name="Databank" /> primarily utilized to ferry passengers across a [[planet]]'s surface, or between an orbiting [[starship]] and a world below.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> [[Neimoidian]] officials in the [[Trade Federation]] used these shuttles for transit from [[battleship]]s to the surface of conquered planets,<ref name="Databank" /> and often preferred models with automatic [[pilot]]s as the absence of a [[cockpit]] allowed for increased passenger space.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" />

[[Viceroy]] [[Nute Gunray]] arrived in [[Theed]] during the Federation [[Invasion of Naboo|occupation of]] [[Naboo]] aboard his personal ''Sheathipede''-class shuttle ''[[Lapiz Cutter]]''. He and his retinue emerged from the vessel's rear hatchway to survey their victory over the [[Naboo (people)|Naboo people]].<ref name="TPM" />

===The Clone Wars===
{{Quote|Ahsoka, Dooku manged to escape. We're in pursuit but we could use reinforcements.|Obi-Wan Kenobi, pursuing Dooku in a stolen ''Sheathipede''-class shuttle|<ref name="Dooku Captured">{{TCW|Dooku Captured}}</ref>}}
[[File:AnakinConfrontsVindi-BSV.png|thumb|right|250px|Anakin Skywalker confronts Nuvo Vindi outside his ''Sheathipede''-class shuttle.]]
Viceroy Gunray continued to make use of these shuttles, and fled [[Geonosis]] following the [[First Battle of Geonosis|outbreak of war]] ten [[Standard year|years]] after the Naboo affair.<ref name="AOTC">{{Film|II}}</ref> He even used a transport ship to land in the planet of [[Rodia]] so he could meet with Senator [[Onaconda Farr]]. However, his transport ship was destroyed by a [[Kwazel Maw]]. [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] later stole [[Unidentified Sheathipede-class transport shuttle (Count Dooku's frigate)|one]] from [[Count Dooku's frigate|Dooku's ''Munificent''-class star frigate]] using it to chase down the [[Sith Lord]]. Although they successfully shot him down over [[Vanqor]], the shuttle was destroyed by a [[Vulture-class starfighter|vulture droid]], and [[Count]] [[Dooku]] escaped only to be captured by a pirate gang led by [[Hondo Ohnaka]] afterward.<ref name="Dooku Captured" /> [[General]] [[Lok Durd]] brought a ''Sheathipede''-class transport shuttle with his forces to [[Maridun]]. The shuttle was left at Durd's [[Separatist outpost (Maridun)|base]] while he and his forces left to [[Defense of Maridun|test]] his [[Defoliator]] weapon on a [[Lurmen village|village]] of [[Lurmen]] colonists, the shuttle was subsequently stolen by a small group of [[Galactic Republic]] [[soldier]]s stranded on the planet who were aware of Durd's presence and intended to stop him.<ref name="Defenders of Peace">{{TCW|Defenders of Peace}}</ref>

[[Doctor]] [[Nuvo Vindi]] maintained a [[Vindi's shuttle|''Sheathipede''-class shuttle]] which was captured by the [[Galactic Republic]] during a [[Raid on Nuvo Vindi's laboratory|raid]] on [[Trade Federation laboratory|his laboratory]] during the [[Blue Shadow Virus]] affair.<ref name="TCW BSV">{{TCW|Blue Shadow Virus (episode)}}</ref><ref name="TCW MoaTM">{{TCW|Mystery of a Thousand Moons}}</ref> During the Battle of Ryloth, a shuttle was assigned to transport Wat Tambor and his droid TA-175, as they knew that Republic forces were going to retake the capital. Not only that, but Dooku wanted Tambor to leave immediately as he would send in Hyena bombers to bomb the capital to demonstrate the cost of a "Republic Victory". Despite Wat Tambor's refusal to retreat until the last of the treasure was boarded, TA-175 was able to leave without him on the shuttle, as Dooku ordered him via hologram to order the Hyena bombers to destroy Lessu immediately. However, Anakin Skywalker and Ahsoka Tano were able to destroy the bombers, allowing Wat Tambor to be captured by Republic forces led by Commander Ponds as well as the [[Twi'lek Resistance]] led by [[Cham Syndulla]].

Another [[Unidentified Sheathipede-class transport shuttle (Cad Bane's frigate)|shuttle]] was parked in [[Cad Bane]]'s [[Cad Bane's Munificent-class star frigate|own ''Munificent''-class star frigate]] during the [[Battle of Devaron]] where it was stolen by Republic forces led by Anakin Skywalker, Ahsoka Tano, Obi Wan Kenobi, and Captain Rex after a failed attempt to recover the [[holocron]] stolen by the bounty hunter. Believing him dead, along with the holocron, it was revealed that Bane was able to fake his death by disguising himself as clone trooper named [[Denal]] and escape in a [[V-19 Torrent starfighter]].<ref name="Cargo of Doom" /> Another [[Unidentified Sheathipede-class transport shuttle (Saleucami)|shuttle]] was also used to recover [[Grievous|General Grievous]] at the [[Battle of Saleucami]].<ref name="Defenders of Peace" />

''Sheathipede''-class shuttles were also parked in the Separatist capital of [[Raxus Secundus]] when Padme and Ahsoka traveled there to set up peace talks with [[Mina Bonteri]], who was an old friend of her.<ref name="HoBS">{{TCW|Heroes on Both Sides}}</ref> One shuttle was also used by [[Mother (title)|Mother]] [[Talzin]] and [[Nightsisters|her]] [[Mother Talzin's clan|clan]] where they went to [[Castle Serenno|Dooku's palace]] in [[Serenno]] to deliver [[Savage Opress]] to him.<ref name="Monster" /> The shuttle may have been a gift from Dooku himself. Another shuttle was also used following the failed [[Skirmish on Naboo]] during a prisoner exchange between Anakin Skywalker and General Grievous. While Anakin was traded to the Gungans, Grievous was exchanged to the Separatists and was able to board the shuttle before it took off along with the remaining Separatist forces.

These shuttles were also parked in [[Mandalore]] during a failed [[Confederate–Republic peace conference|peace conference]] between the Republic and the Separatists. Another shuttle was also used by General Grievous when his fleet attacked Obi Wan Kenobi's fleet.

Following the [[Battle of Coruscant]] in the final days of the [[Clone Wars]], [[General]] [[Grievous]] traveled on a ''Sheathipede''-class transport shuttle to [[Pau City]] on [[Utapau]] to meet with the [[Executive Separatist Council|Separatist Council]].<ref name="ROTS">{{Film|III}}</ref>

===Age of the Empire===
[[File:EzraBridgerSheathipedeClassShuttle-SWX.png|thumb|left|250px|The Spectres named their modified shuttle the ''Phantom II''.]]
Sometime following the Clone Wars, [[Baron]] [[Tarko]] purchased his own ''Sheathipede''-class transport shuttle.<ref name="BMF 54">{{BuildFalconCite|54|Starship Fact File}}</ref> Three ''Sheathipede''-class transport shuttles were present on [[Agamar]] in the wreckage of a Separatist [[Unidentified DH-Omni Support Vessel (Agamar)|supply ship]], where the [[Spectres]] and former Separatist General [[Kalani]]'s [[Agamar garrison|garrison]] used them to escape a [[Mission to Agamar (2 BBY)|battle]] against the [[Galactic Empire]]. One shuttle piloted by droids was shot down in the escape, while the remaining two made it to safety. One contained Kalani and several of his [[B1-series battle droid]]s, and the other one shuttle belonging to the Spectres christened the new ''[[Phantom II]]''.<ref name="The Last Battle" />

The ''Phantom II'' was extensively modified and upgraded by the [[Spectres]]. The shuttle was given a new paint job courtesy of [[Sabine Wren]]. The ship was armed with port and starboard forward-facing cannons and ventral-mounted turrets located adjacent to the boarding ramp.<ref name="Imperial Supercommandos">{{Rebels|Imperial Supercommandos}}</ref> The hull was upgraded with reinforced plating and an [[Astromech droid|astromech]] [[Astromech socket|socket]] located on the shuttle's shortened dorsal fin. It was also modified to dock with the ''[[Ghost]]'' like the original ''[[Phantom]]''.<ref name="Iron Squadron">{{Rebels|Iron Squadron (episode)}}</ref>

===Age of the New Republic===
In the [[New Republic era]], a male [[Neimoidian]] named [[Hallion Nark]] of the [[Warbird gang]] owned a ''Sheathipede''-class transport shuttle, which he landed on [[Jarek Yeager]]'s [[Jarek Yeager's Repair Station|repair shop]] at the ''[[Colossus]]''.<ref name="The Triple Dark" />

==Behind the scenes==
The shuttle was created for its first appearance by [[Industrial Light & Magic|ILM]] employees Larry Tan and [[Adam Savage]] of ''[[Wikipedia:Mythbusters|Mythbusters]]'' fame.<ref>{{YouTube|video=XGFSn2Xm8ks|text=Ask Adam Savage: "Did You Ever Meet George Lucas?"|channel=@tested|name=Adam Savage's Tested|date=2020-05-24}}</ref>

